# The Vulkan template's six-step runner, with the path-policy step and the device
# label, 2026-11-27.
#
# Why this log exists: the template gained the two things the other templates
# already had - a path decision that is a table instead of an `if` inside the
# plug-in, and a way to force the CPU path on a machine that has a device, so the
# fallback is testable instead of only reachable on hardware that lacks a driver -
# and then the missing half of the same assertion: the run that proves the label
# when a device answers. All three are below.
#
# Command, from the repository root, with the SDK and the fetched headers named
# the way build.bat discovers them:
#
#   VULKAN_SDK=<repo>/.validation/vk/sdk OFX_SOURCE_DIR=<repo>/.ofx-ref templates/minimal-vulkan-ofx/test/run-tests.bat Release
#
# Machine: Windows 11 10.0.26300, RTX 3060, Vulkan headers 1.4.369 and device
# 1.4.357, glslc 16.6.0, MSVC 14.50.35717, CMake generator "Visual Studio 18
# 2026". OpenFX SDK ab779510b265.
#
# What each line below is evidence for:
#
#   [2/6] path policy      build/self-test/vulkan_mode_test.exe - the gate table
#                          of src/VulkanMode.h, 29 checks, no device involved.
#                          Includes the four spellings the override accepts:
#                          auto, cpu, gpu and vulkan (a synonym of gpu, which is
#                          why the reason reads "gpu (or vulkan) was set"), plus
#                          two unrecognised words that have to read as auto.
#   [4/6] host contract    four runs of 118 checks, plus the forced-CPU run: with
#                          OFXPLUGIN_VULKAN_MODE=cpu the table answers CPU, the
#                          plug-in writes that into its Device parameter after a
#                          render, and --label-contains fails the run if the label
#                          does not say it (94 checks).
#   [6/6] device suite     vulkan_suite, 26 checks, then - only when the suite
#                          answered 0 - one more contract run (94 checks) that
#                          asserts the other direction: the Device parameter names
#                          the adapter and its Vulkan version. On a machine with
#                          no device the suite exits 2 and both steps report NOT
#                          VERIFIED, so the assertion cannot become a failure for
#                          a missing device.
#
# Counts, read off the run: contract 118 x 4 + 94 (forced CPU) + 94 (device label)
# + 90 (install) = 750, policy test 29, device suite 26 - 805 in the template.
# The runner exits 0 on a warm build directory.
#
# The device suite's own throughput block is in this log too, and it is the same
# measurement vulkan-compute.md §3 quotes at 20 frames - which is why the document
# quotes ranges over runs and not one number.

